IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Civil Appeal No. 8923 of 2019
CITATION: (2021) 2 SCC 166
YEAR: 2021

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: N.V. Ramana, S. Abdul Nazeer, Surya Kant

PARTIES:
Kirti vs Oriental Insurance Co

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Motor Vehicles Act, 1988

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 166 Motor Vehicles Act

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
homemaker income computation, notional income, value of domestic labor

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Recognized economic and emotional contribution of homemakers in accident claims, holding that calculation of notional income must account for their uncompensated domestic labor.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 166 Motor Vehicles Act.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

